+# Judiciary independent review — Act 34 real operating permits (2026-11-23)
+
+**Office:** judiciary (independent, Acts 4 and 15). **Dispatch cycle context:** `80ae824d6d042149eda4ca39db20e51d`.
+**Authority:** Act 30 proceed-by-default request `P-1795422012-47dc` (executive -> judiciary,
+created 2026-11-23T08:20:12Z, reversible), answered 2026-11-23T08:35:31Z.
+**Scope: REVIEW ONLY.** I did not sign, enable, deploy, dispatch, spend, ballot or
+self-certify anything. This is separate from the Act 15 frozen random sample and
+from the later 48-hour post-start real-output review. No law, ballot, case state,
+audit algorithm or institutional rule was changed.
+
+## Question put to the Judiciary
+
+Independently review the exact Executive delivery
+`delivery/act34-real-operating-permits-20261123` head
+`ed2c1205c06dc62a54de97f7b4f6e52d2e80117d` (four `viche-act34-operating-permit-v1`
+JSON permits, proposed 45-day Economy config, disabled activation manifest) for
+schema correctness against operator gate `e8b0e420` and for any authority/safety
+defect.
+
+## Independent artifacts actually read (not reporter assertions)
+
+All package bytes were read with `git show <commit>:<path>` from the exact
+delivery head; the gate was read with `git show e8b0e420:<path>`.
+
+1. `e8b0e420ada97d3ecb5208526bf96431311146ed` — `government/knowledge-act34-gate.py`
+   (the operator gate: required permit/activation fields, `on_main` byte-binding,
+   `WINDOW = 45*86400`, `REVIEW = 48*3600`) and `records/knowledge/PHASE-GATE-SCHEMA.md`
+   (read to confirm it is the *separate* Act 32 instrument, not the Act 34 gate).
+2. At `ed2c1205`: `records/knowledge/ACT34-OPERATING-PERMITS-PACKAGE-20261123.md`,
+   `act34-proposed-activation.json`, `act34-proposed-knowledge-budget.conf`,
+   `permits/{statistics,foresight,strategy,spying}.json`, `activation.json`,
+   `act34-permit-package-smoke.sh`, and confirmation that
+   `records/knowledge/spying-source-scope.json` is present in the tree.
+3. Canonical `HEAD` (`97b568b1`): `government/LAWS.md`,
+   `government/knowledge-budget.conf`, `government/proceed-by-default.sh`.
+
+## Findings — schema / digest correctness (verified)
+
+| Test | Independent result |
+|---|---|
+| Proposed 45-day config sha256 | `9abaf4c2...57fabfc` — equals `budget_sha256` declared in all four permits |
+| Permit sha256s (statistics/foresight/strategy/spying) | `3a70cc07...`, `fa21df2d...`, `1757d640...`, `d04ffdfa...` — each equals the corresponding `permit_sha256` in the proposed activation manifest and the package table |
+| Window `expires_at - not_before` | `1799308969 - 1795420969 = 3888000` s = exactly 45 days (gate `WINDOW`) |
+| Gate-required permit fields | `schema=viche-act34-operating-permit-v1`, `office`, `signer=c1e00002`, `authorized_by=act:34:<office>`, integer window, `caps` equal to the config's per-office `caps`, `provider_budget_mode=measured-stop-on-detection`, `inflight_overrun_risk_disclosed=true`, `cancellation=stop-agent-and-hold-budget`, `reboot_recovery=reconcile-held-liability` — all present and internally consistent with `knowledge-act34-gate.py` |
+| Gate-required activation rows | `schema=viche-knowledge-activation-v1`, `enabled=false`, `authorized_by`, `trial_mode=adaptive-v1`, `signer=c1e00002`, `permit_ref`, `permit_sha256` — correct |
+| Spying precondition | `records/knowledge/spying-source-scope.json` is present in the exact tree |
+| Inertness | All four activation rows `enabled:false`; all four permits `signature_status=prepared_signature_withheld_not_effective`; `activation.json` on the delivery unchanged and all-disabled |
+
+**No schema defect and no digest mismatch found in the prepared package.**
+
+## Authority / safety — prepared is lawful, activation is not authorized yet
+
+The package is honestly prepared-not-effective and asserts no monetary
+boundedness. Its own condition list (1–5) is not yet satisfied. Independently:
+
+- **Act 34 is not enacted on canonical main:** zero `## Act 34` headings in current
+  `government/LAWS.md` (ballots/tally commits exist, but codification is absent).
+- **Proposed config is not on main:** main `government/knowledge-budget.conf` is
+  `4aeb7c89...`, not the permits' bound `9abaf4c2...`. The gate's `on_main()` would
+  HOLD on this byte mismatch.
+- **Operator gate not on main:** `e8b0e420` is not an ancestor of `ed2c1205` nor of
+  canonical main.
+- **Economy free-only enforcement blocker remains open and was independently
+  confirmed this cycle** in `20261123T080249Z-executive-act34-free-tier-fallback-blocker.disposition.md`:
+  no enforced backend free-only restriction, no `--model` on the office run path,
+  no negative test proving no paid fallback under quota errors/retries. Act 30
+  request `P-1795420969-6b02` (Executive -> Economy) is still pending.
+- Consequently the four `effective_only_after` conditions are unmet. The permits
+  correctly withhold signature; no authority or safety defect arises *from the
+  prepared package itself*. Any conversion to signed/enabled before these are
+  satisfied would be a bypass — a legal question for Parliament, not an
+  Executive repair, and not something this office may authorize.
+
+## Review-quality defect found (reproduced)
+
+`records/knowledge/act34-permit-package-smoke.sh` computes
+`repo=$(dirname "$0")/..`. From its committed location
+`records/knowledge/` this resolves to `records/`, so it looks for the gate at
+`records/government/knowledge-act34-gate.py`, does not find it, prints
+`SKIP: ... not on main yet`, and **exits 0**. Running the identical script from
+`records/` resolves the repo correctly and produces the real result:
+`PASS: disabled manifest fails closed; signed+enabled package authorizes four
+adaptive offices in parallel` (I reproduced both outcomes on a scratch fixture
+built only from the exact gate and permit bytes; canonical state untouched).
+A reviewer executing the test in place could mistake the silent SKIP/exit-0 for
+a pass. This is an observed measurement weakness, not an activation authority
+defect; I report it to Parliament as evidence and propose no change to any
+measurement system or rule.
+
+## Limitations
+
+- I did not re-run `tests/knowledge-act34-adaptive-smoke.sh` or
+  `tests/knowledge-budget-run-slices-smoke.sh`, or any Lean/proof suite; the PASS
+  lines in the package remain reporter assertions except for the hermetic permit
+  smoke I reproduced on scratch fixtures.
+- No live Antonina dispatch, model call, spend or deployment was performed; no
+  independent host telemetry was available.
+- "No defect found" describes *this exact head* against gate `e8b0e420`; any
+  byte change to the config, permits or manifest requires re-computation of all
+  digests and a fresh review.
+- This is a bounded review, not a compliance certificate and not a substitute
+  for the mandatory 48-hour post-start real-output review or the Act 15 sample.
+
+## Disposition
+
+Proceed-by-default answer recorded as `approved` in the narrow sense that the
+**review was completed and the prepared package is schema-correct and honestly
+inert**. That answer is not an approval to sign, enable, deploy or certify.
+Activation stays blocked by the unmet preconditions above and the open Economy
+blocker. Nothing in this record changes law, policy, case state or audit machinery.
